1
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,530
Kirito.

2
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,260
Yeah, Alne?

3
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,500
Listen, I have faith in
your skills as a swordsman,

4
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,140
but I have to warn you about something.

5
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,820
The Levantains have a saying,
handed down for generations.

6
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:43,017
Soak your sword in the
blood of the mighty,

7
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,982
and you will make their
strength become your own.

8
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,920
Like blood, blood? Yes.

9
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,740
Before he started here,

10
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:56,413
Volo had been engaging in first-strike
duels with real swords for a while.

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,441
As a result of that, those experiences
are what gave him his power.

12
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,220
His imagination, of course.

13
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:07,617
Volo's strength is tied to an
old family motto he grew up with.

14
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:12,560
So if he beats someone strong, he
believes he'll get stronger from it.

15
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,150
Watch out.

16
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:18,572
He aims to draw blood today so he can
wet his blade and grow even stronger.

17
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,420
I know you can do this.

18
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,440
I have the utmost faith in you.

19
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:29,722
You are not the type of swordsman
who would fall so easily to him.

20
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:34,227
Also, this is the perfect
opportunity to fulfill your promise.

21
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,700
What promise?

22
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,533
Oh, yeah, I said I'd show you
the best sword skill I had.

23
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,040
That's right, so show
it to me here, on him.

24
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:45,990
Done.

25
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:47,544
You'll see the best one I know.

26
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,180
Shall we start, trainee Kirito?

27
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,170
Yeah.

28
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:05,040
Elite Disciple Surlute, will you
serve as witness to this duel?

29
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,320
Yes, of course.

30
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:13,980
Elite Disciple Leventain
versus Primary Trainee Kirito.

31
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:17,335
The victor shall be the one
who lands the first strike.

32
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:23,960
Let it be known that both parties have
agreed to use real swords in this match.

33
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:26,670
Let's go,

34
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:36,040
let's

35
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,270
go.

36
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:52,077
This is the end of the
day, and it's a great day?

37
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:52,990
and it's a great day.

38
00:02:53,073 --> 00:02:54,780
It's a part of the end of the day.

39
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:02,107
I hope that the power is on.

40
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,477
I hope that the hope is
on the end of the day.

41
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,390
I hope that the fire is off.

42
00:03:04,473 --> 00:03:05,303
We will be fine.

43
00:03:05,386 --> 00:03:10,460
I hope that the power is on the end.

44
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,417
It's epic!

45
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:20,417
It makes me a voice See you
livez in yourself My first

46
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:26,480
time I will see you with
eternal life I will be upon you

47
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:34,637
SHINING STORM MAN DIAMOND Happy
to be the red person Turnin

48
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:32,397
Oh my word, I didn't know painting
swords black was a custom in the boonies.

49
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,820
Did you, Lord Rios?

50
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:36,240
Don't be so insensitive, Umber.

51
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:41,366
It's not the poor Page's fault he's too
busy to polish the filth from his sword.

52
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,680
A mountain-splitting wave
of the High-Norkian style.

53
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,060
He's starting with his best skill.

54
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,500
That's Avalanche.

55
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:14,520
A heavy one-hit thrust.

56
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,760
But it's the hardcore version of it.

57
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:21,160
His imagination's boosting its power.

58
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,680
Dodging's not an option.

59
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,090
No.

60
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,399
I'm gonna have to block his strike.

61
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,720
I gotta promise to keep.

62
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:37,180
I have to counter with something bigger,
like the four-part vertical square.

63
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,180
He blocked it!

64
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:19,900
If I can hold out, I can
still get my fourth hidden!

65
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,180
Holy crap!

66
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:28,580
Is that the source of his power?

67
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:39,140
He's picturing his
ancestors, backing him up.

68
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:46,760
I won't lose to him.

69
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,100
No way.

70
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,660
I can't.

71
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:59,000
I'm not going to let you beat me.

72
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:16,060
Did his sword just grow?

73
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:46,960
That is enough!

74
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,580
Ms. Zuzurka?

75
00:07:58,700 --> 00:08:02,660
If she decides the duel
is over, we must obey her.

76
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:05,670
Um, okay.

77
00:08:05,753 --> 00:08:06,900
But why, though?

78
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,390
Years ago,

79
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:11,446
during the Four Empire
Unification Tournament,

80
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:15,220
she was the first swordsman to
represent North Norlingarth.

81
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:19,600
Trainee Kirito's punishment
is hereby fulfilled!

82
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,940
Next time, try not to
fling mud onto anyone.

83
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,540
You were lucky today.

84
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,200
It's back to normal.

85
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,720
I thought you had been slashed

86
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,260
Yeah, talk about close, huh?

87
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,457
Anyone else would have surrendered.

88
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:04,940
Oh, you hopeless fool!

89
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:11,397
That said, it was a magnificent fight.

90
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,380
Well done.

91
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,920
I am forever grateful.

92
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,724
On the one hand, I wish
I could have fought you?

93
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:24,362
But on the other, you did keep your promise
and showed me what you were capable of.

94
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:25,490
Nicely done.

95
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,700
But, um, nobody won. It was a draw.

96
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:33,580
Is achieving a draw against the first
seat not good enough for you? Uh, no.

97
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,140
That's not what I meant. I hope not.

98
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,977
The result wasn't even the point.

99
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,817
Seeing you fight was, actually.

100
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,253
It taught me something.

101
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,925
Something extremely important.

102
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:48,213
We can talk about it back at
my place while we celebrate.

103
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:51,540
We'll invite you, Gio,
and Lord Golgorosso, too.

104
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,530
Sure.

105
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:12,740
As I was watching your
match, it hit me again.

106
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:16,137
Your Aincrad style has
limitless possibilities.

107
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:21,920
As for the surlude style, I once saw it
as a practical skill, but it's too stiff.

108
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:23,170
Oh, come on.

109
00:10:23,253 --> 00:10:24,177
Don't go there again.

110
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:27,319
I haven't beaten you a
single time since I got here.

111
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,234
Surlude style's attacks are so diverse.

112
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,028
In my book, that's what
makes it so amazing.

113
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,520
It's history as two. How?

114
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:43,457
Once, a distant ancestor of mine
angered the Emperor at the time.

115
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,716
And because of that,

116
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:49,487
the Sir Lute family was banished from
the official Hynorkia style indefinitely.

117
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,710
Oh.

118
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,940
So my family improvised.

119
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,748
And then, from that, our
non-traditional style was developed,

120
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,860
becoming the Sir Lute style.

121
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,340
I don't resent it by any means.

122
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:04,855
On the contrary, I have always
been proud of our style.

123
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:10,389
Still, I may have retained some
doubts about its legitimacy.

124
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,100
These two years,

125
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:17,341
I couldn't beat Volo, not because
he specialized in a better style,

126
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:19,560
but because I felt mine was lesser.

127
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,030
Lina...

128
00:11:22,113 --> 00:11:25,920
You and I though, we both have
unique styles of swordplay.

129
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:31,301
The difference is, you don't feel inferior
to those trained in more orthodox styles.

130
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:35,497
After watching you this past year,

131
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:39,720
and seeing how you fought with
Volo in today's duel, To be honest,

132
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,999
I think I understand why you don't.

133
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:43,420
For me,

134
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:48,860
knowing I'm the successor to the Sir Lute's
style fills me with great pride and joy.

135
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,808
There is no better feeling.

136
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:54,525
Becoming your mentor is
a close second, though.

137
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,280
Thanks, Lina.

138
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:59,231
And now that you saw how I countered Volo,

139
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:03,360
you shouldn't have any trouble
beating him in the finals. Right.

140
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,100
Oh, well, well, what perfect timing.

141
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:31,440
I was hoping I'd run into
you, and here you are.

142
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,500
What do you guys want?

143
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:39,708
Well, naturally, I wanted to commend you
on your dazzling performance earlier.

144
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:40,930
True.

145
00:12:41,013 --> 00:12:43,249
Those were some very
flashy-looking skills.

146
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:48,060
I'm certain you unnerved first-seat
Leventayne with your dashing theatrics.

147
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,828
Woody, you pick in a fight?

148
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,037
Certainly not.

149
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:57,560
A nobleman would never dare engage in
uncouth activities with a commoner.

150
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,640
Unless it's giving handouts.

151
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:09,960
To praise your stunt, no, to
honor your battle, here is a gift.

152
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:11,400
No need to thank me.

153
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,820
It is my one charitable act for the day.

154
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,960
Good night, Sir Kirito.

155
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,360
Sir nothing!

156
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:51,320
It started out as an experiment.

157
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:59,481
The Zephylia is a type of flower that doesn't
bloom anywhere in the Northern Empire.

158
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:02,092
Lena told me that they were her favorite.

159
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,070
it.

160
00:14:04,153 --> 00:14:07,837
I tried to make them bloom,
using my imagination theory.

161
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:12,320
And along the way, I started
identifying with the flowers,

162
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:16,640
because I knew how hard it
was trying to stay alive in a

163
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:19,510
foreign place.

164
00:14:19,593 --> 00:14:22,957
Having been cut off from the real
world and all the people I loved

165
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:27,680
and cared for made me feel more and
more alone as time went on here.

166
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,420
I shared that pain with these flowers.

167
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,100
I'm sorry.

168
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,500
Have faith.

169
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,417
Believe in the strength of the flowers.

170
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,177
You grew in this foreign soil.

171
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:05,420
Who's there?

172
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:10,840
Believe in yourself, too, for helping
them grow as well as they have.

173
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:16,820
Yeah, but it didn't matter in the end.

174
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,700
Worry not.

175
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:22,120
Their roots still cling
to life within the soil.

176
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,980
You sense it, do you not?

177
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:29,580
The sacred flowers in this garden
want to save their friends.

178
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,908
Their energy shall aid you.

179
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,440
But how?

180
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:39,160
I don't know any of the
spells that can help.

181
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:41,578
You do not need to.

182
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,440
The arts are only tools to
harness and refine the meaning,

183
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,160
or what you call the mental image.

184
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:50,640
Use your heart.

185
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:55,040
Feel the prayers of the
flowers, the ways of the world.

186
00:15:56,520 --> 00:16:00,060
Feel the prayers of the
flowers, the meaning.

187
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,620
Please, help me.

188
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,714
I need you to share some of your power.

189
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:40,480
Imagine the flower's life force flowing
through you and into the Zephelia's roots.

190
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:19,360
Whoever you are, thanks a lot.

191
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:30,450
Ah!

192
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,900
Oh, my God.

193
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,600
Heeey!

194
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,940
Oh...

195
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:48,620
Match over!

196
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:11,920
Lina graduated from the North
Senator Swordcraft Academy.

197
00:19:13,980 --> 00:19:16,780
She was the top-ranked student that year.

198
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:21,400
After our advancement exam,

199
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,397
Eugeo and me were ranked seat 5 and 6?

200
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:27,080
and got promoted to elite disciples.

201
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:32,960
Elite Disciple Eugeo, I am here to report.

202
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:36,560
The assigned cleaning has been completed.

203
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,540
Thanks, Tiese. Good work.

204
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:42,113
I don't have anything else
for you, so you're free to go.

205
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:45,060
Oh, and, um…

206
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,480
I'm sorry, Ronie.

207
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:53,657
I don't know how many times I've told him
to be back before you finish cleaning,

208
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:54,975
but he never listens.

209
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,170
It's fine.

210
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:59,537
I'll just wait until he comes
back so I can make my report.

211
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:00,450
You know,

212
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:01,363
if you really want,

213
00:20:01,446 --> 00:20:05,297
I can always put in a good word so you can
get your mentor changed to someone else.

214
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:08,717
You're going to have a really
long year if you serve under him.

215
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:09,682
Just a warning.

216
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,320
Oh, I don't mind.

217
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,150
I knew it.

218
00:20:13,233 --> 00:20:15,880
You guys were talking
about me behind my back.

219
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:21,220
Um, Elate Disciple
Kirito, here's my report.

220
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:22,815
Cleaning is complete.

221
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:26,337
Everything is shiny and
spotless. Oh, okay. Thanks.

222
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:27,920
Come on, Kirito.

223
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:31,357
These two have a lot on their
plate, so please respect that.

224
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:34,377
At least try to get back here
before they're done cleaning.

225
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:37,937
And could you tell me why you're coming
in through the window all of a sudden?

226
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:40,617
Because it's the shortest
route from East Third Street.

227
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,197
It's way faster than
going through the lobby.

228
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:46,817
Keep that in mind, because on days
you're running late, it's a lifesaver.

229
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:47,800
Oh, right!

230
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:49,985
Could you not teach them that?

231
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:54,797
Hang on, if you're coming from East
Third, then that bag is from...

232
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:59,360
Ha, so much for manners when your
stomach's rumbling, eh, Yu-Gi-Oh?

233
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:01,690
Here.

234
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:09,685
Here, I bought extra so you can
share some with your dorm mates.

235
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,680
Thank you so much, Ely Disciple Kirito!

236
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:19,697
We'll head back as fast as we can and
eat these before their life decreases.

237
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:21,133
We'll see you tomorrow!

238
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:26,314
Oh, it's full of honey pies
from the Prancing Deer Cafe.

239
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,701
Let's hurry before they get cold.

240
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:33,990
What's up?

241
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:36,360
Oh, nothing much, really.

242
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:40,080
It's just, I'm wondering
where your head's at.

243
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:42,537
I hope you haven't gotten
so comfortable lately that

244
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:45,738
you've forgotten why we came
here in the first place.

245
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,080
Like I'd forget.

246
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:51,240
We're closer now than ever.

247
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,060
Almost there.

248
00:22:58,620 --> 00:23:03,360
I have no pain left,
and I have no pain left.

249
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:09,240
It's not your face, it's not your eyes.

250
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,999
If you feel like you're next to me,

251
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:19,037
I have no pain left.

252
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:24,320
